draw first two chars from [a-z0-9] (36 symbols), not [0-9a-f]; jira ids all begin 'ji'","AC #1 asserts >=80% top-level tree shrink on a fixture single-ticket mutation, but the distribution of a real 6,008-id store depends entirely on this derivation being uniform"],"finding":"The shard-key derivation is described as '<first-two-hex>' but canonical ticket ids are not hex: native ids match [a-z0-9]{4}(-[a-z0-9]{4}){3} (first two chars range over [a-z0-9], e.g. an id starting 'zx'/'gg') and Jira ids match jira-<project>-<number> (so every Jira ticket's first two chars are 'ji'). Taken literally, 'first-two-hex' misnames the domain, and a naive first-two-chars-of-id scheme places ALL jira-* tickets in one 'ji' shard, defeating fan-out for a Jira-heavy store.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9fea89f5650c5df7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('tickets/<first-two-hex>/<id>') and Implementation Plan step 1 (ticket_layout shard/relpath derivation)","norm_id":"ne7390da38e741a4c","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store dominated by jira-<project>-<num> ids collapses into the single 'ji' shard, so per-commit root-tree churn is barely reduced","An implementer reads 'hex' literally and builds a 16- or 256-way scheme that cannot represent ids beginning with g-z"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the derivation explicitly — e.g. shard = first two chars of sha256(canonical_id).hexdigest() (uniform 256-way fan-out independent of id grammar, so jira-* ids spread evenly), owned solely by ticket_layout; or, if keeping an id-prefix scheme, document that native ids span [a-z0-9] and add an explicit rule so jira-* ids do not all land in one shard.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_sa