-file inventory for the flat-ticket-path routing is incomplete: it omits four _commands modules that construct tracker/<resolved-id> ticket-dir paths directly. composer.py builds `pdir = tracker / resolved` and checks `(tracker / resolved).is_dir()` (parent-existence gate), leaf.py builds `ticket_dir = tracker / resolved` and iterdir()/reduce_ticket()s it (archive), composer_edit.py does `reduce_ticket(str(tracker / resolved))`, and link_revert.py builds `ticket_dir = tracker / resolved`. None appear in the plan's commands list, whose known failure mode (silent omission) is exactly this.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb0a83409d6fbb0f8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan, step 4 — commands `{_seam,claim,transition,transition_close,txn,delete,recent_creates,completion_candidate,compact,...,verify_authorship}.py`","norm_id":"nb96b3b39d54d91e0","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["_commands/composer.py: parent-existence check `(tracker / resolved).is_dir()` returns False for a sharded parent, so child/create rejects valid parents as 'does not exist'.","_commands/leaf.py archive(): `tracker / resolved` no longer names the sharded ticket dir, so `.archived`/ARCHIVED detection and reduce_ticket() misfire and archive fails or double-writes.","_commands/composer_edit.py: `reduce_ticket(str(tracker / resolved))` reads an empty/nonexistent flat dir, so tag-delta and state reads on edit return wrong state.","_commands/link_revert.py: `ticket_dir = tracker / resolved` points at a nonexistent flat path, breaking link revert on migrated stores."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Route the `tracker / resolved` ticket-dir joins in composer.py (185-187), leaf.py (207), composer_edit.py (104,137), and link_revert.py (270) through the ticket_layout existing-dir resolver, and re-run find_referencing_symbols on the resolver/join site (plus a string grep for `tracker / ` and `os.path.join(tracker`) to confirm no further command modules are missed.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how tickets written at sharded paths after the migration commit are handled on rollback, and assert on the post-rollback resolvable state of those tickets (not merely that the reverted flat store is readable).","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'rollback is a tickets-branch revert or approved tracker-maintenance action that restores flat paths and removes the capability stamp together; tests assert the reverted flat store remains readable by intended binaries.'","The rollback assertion covers only the reverted flat store's readability, not post-migration sharded writes layered on top of the migration commit.","POST-ROLLBACK STATE applicability: the plan rewrites persisted records in place (renames) and narrows/adds a read path via the compat token, so it must assert on state AFTER rollback, not merely that rollback completed."],"finding":"The rollback path for an already-migrated store does not assert on the fate of tickets created or mutated at sharded paths AFTER the migration commit but before rollback; a tickets-branch revert of the migration commit could restore flat paths while later sharded-path commits remain on top.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb20d28b58820da7f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Deployment / Rollback section","norm_id":"nc5edc64c50ec4ede","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator migrates a store, agents create new tickets that land at tickets/<shard>/<id>, then the operator reverts the migration commit and downgrades binaries.","A plain revert of only the migration commit leaves post-migration sharded tickets at shard paths while the reverted binary may resolve only flat paths."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that rollback must relocate any post-migration sharded ticket dirs back to flat paths (e.g. a compensating tracker-maintenance action rather than a bare git revert of the migration commit), and add a test that a store with tickets created after migration remains fully resolvable by the reverted binary.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"non