-store fan-out and briefly justify the 2-hex shard width for the ~6k-ticket scale.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Implement a fan-out layout tickets/<first-two-hex>/<id> for canonical ticket ids.'","Step 9 commits to documenting 'shard derivation' but does not cite the git object-store precedent or the shard-width rationale.","Web search confirmed the first-two-hex-char subdirectory scheme is git's canonical loose-object layout and a standard content-addressed-store technique — established prior art, not a novel pattern."],"finding":"The plan borrows git's own loose-object-store fan-out pattern (tickets/<first-two-hex>/<id> == .git/objects/ab/cdef...) but never names this prior art nor justifies the 2-hex shard-width choice against alternatives (e.g., deeper fan-out, different bucket widths, or directory-lookup sharding). Because this is a well-trodden pattern the pattern choice needs no search, but the design rationale (why mirror git's scheme, why 2 hex chars for ~6k tickets) is undocumented.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa8a5b2f8fded39df","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 9; Scope ('fan-out layout tickets/<first-two-hex>/<id>')","norm_id":"nbfdeb75eecdac926","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer questioning why 2 hex chars (256 buckets) was chosen for a ~6k-ticket store, or considering re-sharding.","Reviewers assessing whether the layout is novel or a known-good pattern."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the architecture/migrations doc noting the layout follows git's established .git/objects/<2-hex> sharding precedent and stating why 256 buckets suit the current/projected ticket count.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","cla